NXR-241|UART whole-record atomicity|Driver qualification|Queued UART qualification shall prove that concurrent producer records never interleave within a record across partial transport writes.|The queued implementation preserves pending offsets but needs sustained concurrent transport evidence.|Three seeded producers emit counted records through one-byte writes; each complete record belongs to one producer and sequence.|Compare exact output with an independent record parser while forcing full and busy transport responses.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Configured static record slots and message size; no producer waits for device readiness.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|The queued implementation preserves pending offsets but needs sustained concurrent transport evidence.
NXR-242|UART acceptance accounting|Driver qualification|UART counters shall distinguish accepted, rejected-full, truncated, transmitted and failed records.|A hello demo cannot establish that overload and truncation are visible to callers.|Saturate the queue and formatting limit; every producer attempt has one documented outcome and byte conservation reconciles.|Use known record lengths and controlled transport errors with counter boundary fixtures.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Saturating diagnostic counters; fixed queue capacity.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|A hello demo cannot establish that overload and truncation are visible to callers.
NXR-243|UART boot and BSP contract|Driver qualification|UART initialization shall declare device base, clock, reset, baud and ordered-MMIO guarantees before the service worker runs.|The current AXI TX adapter intentionally does not initialize clocks, baud or reset.|Misaligned base and wrong device profile are rejected; measured pin baud matches the configured tolerance.|Combine address-validation host fixtures with board clock and pin-loopback measurements.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|No runtime driver discovery; one permanent owner per configured UART.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|The current AXI TX adapter intentionally does not initialize clocks, baud or reset.
NXR-244|UART receiver overrun policy|Driver qualification|A future UART receiver shall expose bounded storage, per-error counters and a documented record resynchronization rule.|The supplied AXI adapter is TX-only and must not be described as a complete RX or interrupt driver.|Overflow during a stalled reader does not corrupt adjacent memory and subsequent delimiter-framed packets recover.|Inject framing errors, bursts beyond capacity and consumer pauses on real hardware.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed RX ring and finite ISR work per entry; no heap.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|The supplied AXI adapter is TX-only and must not be described as a complete RX or interrupt driver.
NXR-245|External interrupt acknowledgement|Driver qualification|Peripheral IRQ qualification shall establish source identification, acknowledgement order and pending recheck without losing a concurrent event.|Current timer-only dispatch cannot establish a working UART or DMA external interrupt path.|An event arriving during acknowledgement is eventually serviced once; spurious sources do not call unrelated handlers.|Use hardware-generated edge and level stimuli and an independent event count.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed handler table; bounded per-entry service and declared nesting policy.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|Current timer-only dispatch cannot establish a working UART or DMA external interrupt path.
NXR-246|Interrupt storm containment|Driver qualification|The BSP shall contain a continuously asserted peripheral source without permanently starving the scheduling timer.|Acknowledging a misbehaving device indefinitely can turn bounded driver code into scheduler starvation.|Hold a level source active; the declared mask or defer policy activates and timer progress remains observable.|Inject a stuck source while measuring timer and high-priority worker progress externally.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Finite events-per-entry budget and bounded deferred queue.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|Acknowledging a misbehaving device indefinitely can turn bounded driver code into scheduler starvation.
NXR-247|GPIO ownership and register races|Driver qualification|GPIO qualification shall prove pin ownership and correct atomic set-clear semantics under concurrent unrelated pin updates.|Generic volatile access alone does not protect shared GPIO read-modify-write operations.|Two threads toggle disjoint pins without lost updates; conflicting ownership is rejected before register access.|Capture pins externally and exercise write-one and read-modify-write register variants.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed pin table; critical section limit declared for non-atomic hardware.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|Generic volatile access alone does not protect shared GPIO read-modify-write operations.
NXR-248|Watchdog progress quorum|Driver qualification|Watchdog feeding shall require progress from every mandatory worker in the current supervision epoch.|A heartbeat from one healthy monitor cannot establish overall scheduler or application progress.|Freeze one required worker while the monitor stays alive; feeding stops and the declared reset is observed.|Inject worker stalls at differing priorities and compare independent reset timing.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed worker bitmap and finite epoch; optional workers explicitly excluded.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|A heartbeat from one healthy monitor cannot establish overall scheduler or application progress.
NXR-249|SPI transaction cancellation|Driver qualification|SPI cancellation shall retain chip select and buffer ownership until the controller is demonstrably quiescent.|A mutex around submission alone does not serialize the full hardware transaction lifetime.|Cancel mid-transfer and on completion boundary; no new client begins before settled bus ownership.|Observe chip select and clock while injecting completion delay and controller faults.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed transaction slots and finite cancellation deadline; uncertain hardware quarantined.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|A mutex around submission alone does not serialize the full hardware transaction lifetime.
NXR-250|I2C stuck-bus recovery evidence|Driver qualification|I2C recovery shall use a board-declared bounded procedure and report failure when SCL or SDA cannot be released.|Recovery must be based on actual line state and board electrical constraints.|NACK, clock stretching and permanently low lines yield distinct terminal outcomes without indefinite polling.|Use programmable pull-down fixtures and capture recovery pulses and stop generation.|NXR-041,NXR-119,NXR-149|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Finite stretch and recovery pulse limits; no unconditional bus-reset loops.|include/rtos_uart.hpp,docs/drivers.rst,tests/uart.cpp|Recovery must be based on actual line state and board electrical constraints.
